  <bpmn:process id="Process_38" name="Capacity and Scheduling Rule Configuration" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>Sources: docs/proposed-bpmn-catalog.md BPMN-38, related processes and reuse rules; Chapters/Kitchen406 - Capstone Paper.md SRS FR-CAP-01-13,19-21 and FR-SUB-05; supporting NFR-SEC-03,08, NFR-REL-03,05-06. Website: index.html loads app/capacity-state.js Q.save/block/saveSchedule/preserveSchedule, app/owner-scheduling.js configuration and blocked-date warnings, app/scheduling.js and app/owner-subscriptions.js. Reviewed existing BPMN-06/09/15/37 conventions and catalog ownership. The SRS is authoritative: current preview accepts generic hour/day lead values and configurable cake daily capacity; proposed validation must preserve mandatory noon/day rules, seven-calendar-day cake submission lead and distinct cake fulfillment dates. Configurable baselines do not erase existing allocations. Input: Owner authenticated by BPMN-30, current configuration version and one requested settings/block/unblock/subscription-schedule change. Output: current future-facing rules saved while commitments are preserved, or correction/retry/cancellation. Separate capacity pools apply by fulfillment date: standard daily varieties/units; subscription weekly per product; cake weekly with distinct fulfillment dates. Existing prepaid preparation/fulfillment schedules are snapshotted/preserved when settings or offering schedules change. This bounded process does not invoke checkout reservation, release a hold, create paid fulfillments, take payment or apply customer deferment. BPMN-09 consumes configured rules, BPMN-06 checks permitted deferment capacity, BPMN-03 displays offerings and BPMN-04 retains agreed confirmed schedule. These are references to completed/downstream ownership, not calls of their whole workflows. No currently authored BPMN defines a global configuration validator, so local validation is explicit rather than an unresolved call. Internal Owner/System lanes use sequence flows; no external messaging is necessary. Recoverable errors keep a visible review/edit/retry/stop route, with stale configuration reloaded for review before resubmission. Proposed reliability safeguards are process behavior, not a claim every UI/backend control already exists.</bpmn:documentation>
