    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start_38" name="Owner opens capacity/scheduling configuration">
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_38_1</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Load_38" name="Check Owner access; load current rules, version and commitments">
      <bpmn:documentation>Require Admin/Owner; read independent pool limits, timing rules, blocked dates/reasons, subscription product schedule/status and current active/held allocations for context. Existing schedule snapshots must not be discarded. Staff cannot configure these rules.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_38_28</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_38_1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_38_2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Allowed_38" name="Owner access/load successful?">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_38_2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_38_3</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_38_5</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="AccessError_38" name="Explain permission/load issue; retain configuration">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_38_3</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_38_4</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="AccessEnd_38" name="Configuration not opened; no changes">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_38_4</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:userTask id="Edit_38" name="Edit pool limits/timing, block/unblock a date, or maintain offering schedule">
      <bpmn:documentation>Choose applicable change. Edit separate baselines and timing rather than one shared capacity total. Blocking includes valid date and supported reason (prototype reason category/details); unblocking removes only that block. Subscription schedule maintenance selects eligible product, preparation/fulfillment weekdays and active/inactive status. Deactivation affects new enrollment, not ongoing prepaid subscriptions. Preserve unrelated fields. Defaults: standard four varieties/day and ten units/variety; subscription ten/product/week; cake two/week with distinct dates, subject to permitted owner baseline changes.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_38_25</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_38_16</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_38_5</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_38_6</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:userTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Confirm_38" name="Owner submits/confirms changes?">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_38_6</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_38_7</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_38_8</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="Cancel_38" name="Cancelled; prior settings and commitments retained">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_38_7</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:businessRuleTask id="Validate_38" name="Validate selected configuration, separate pools and mandatory timing rules">
      <bpmn:documentation>FR-CAP-01-13,19-21. Recognize requested settings/block/unblock/schedule operation and validate applicable fields/targets only. Baselines are positive whole counts; standard daily varieties and units/variety, subscription weekly units/product, cake weekly count with each cake assigned a distinct fulfillment date. Timing values/units and times must be valid; interpret business times in Asia/Manila. Standard latest permitted cutoff is noon at least one day before fulfillment, or an earlier product-specific preparation deadline. Subscription noon cutoff is at least one day before first preparation based on product lead time. Cake requests need at least seven calendar days before fulfillment; timely submitted request does not become late solely during review. Configurable rules may reflect stricter applicable preparation needs but cannot override mandatory SRS constraints. Validate blocked date/reason and subscription product/weekdays/status; do not invent mandatory preparation-to-delivery offset or fixed calendar dates beyond SRS. Unknown/missing target is a correction issue.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_38_8</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_38_9</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:businessRuleTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Valid_38" name="Configuration and mandatory rules valid?">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_38_9</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_38_10</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_38_11</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="InputError_38" name="Explain invalid field/rule; keep draft and saved settings">
      <bpmn:documentation>Display the specific capacity, date, target or cutoff/lead violation. Existing rules/allocations unchanged. Correct the same draft and resubmit or stop; do not silently normalize an invalid business rule.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_38_10</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_38_22</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:businessRuleTask id="Impact_38" name="Evaluate new-booking impact and protect existing commitments">
      <bpmn:documentation>FR-SUB-05; FR-CAP-10-13. Compare proposed limits/blocks/schedule changes with active allocations and confirmed subscription schedule snapshots. Lower capacity or blocking a committed date is not permission to cancel/release/move existing work. Existing allocations may exceed new baseline; future booking checks then show no available capacity until allowed by current commitments. Preserve agreed subscription preparation/fulfillment dates and existing original quantities/amounts; configuration/schedule deactivation applies prospectively. Do not require no existing commitments as an invented save condition. Detect inconsistent record/config version for safe review.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_38_11</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_38_12</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:businessRuleTask>
    <bpmn:userTask id="ImpactReview_38" name="Review affected dates/limits; confirm preserved work or revise/cancel">
      <bpmn:documentation>Show impact including already scheduled work and any over-limit condition. Existing work remains due as agreed. This review is not approval to reschedule paid commitments. Prototype shows a warning when blocking a date with preparation/fulfillment and states lower limits preserve allocations. For changes without affected work, review simply confirms prospective scope.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_38_12</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_38_13</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:userTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="ImpactConfirmed_38" name="Keep proposed change?">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_38_13</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_38_14</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_38_15</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Decision_38" name="Revise or stop?">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_38_15</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_38_16</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_38_17</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Save_38" name="Recheck version/access; preserve snapshots and save future rules consistently">
      <bpmn:documentation>Recheck Owner permission, current configuration and applicable target/dependency version, current mandatory-rule validity and commitments at commit. Preserve confirmed subscription schedule snapshots before changing mutable defaults or offering records. Save only requested pool/timing/block/unblock/schedule operation and related metadata/version consistently. Retain allocation identities/status, original dates/amounts and unrelated rules. Reject stale update without overwriting independently committed newer state. Failed combined update commits no partial setting/snapshot mutation. Safe repeated submission cannot duplicate a schedule/block; known matching saved operation returns its saved result. No hold release, refund, auto deferment or resource reservation.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_38_14</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_38_18</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Saved_38" name="Settings saved or matching result retained?">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_38_18</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_38_19</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_38_20</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="SaveError_38" name="Explain conflict/save failure; preserve current settings and draft">
      <bpmn:documentation>On stale version, reload current data and explicitly review/reconcile draft before retry. On transient failure retry only after current controls revalidate. Preserve newer independent changes and existing commitments. No partial configuration/snapshot update.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_38_19</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_38_23</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Refresh_38" name="Show saved rules, blocked dates and preserved work for future checks">
      <bpmn:documentation>Display saved baselines/timing/blocks/offering schedule and existing work, including over-limit state if applicable. New bookings use available capacity by fulfillment date; blocked/full dates cannot be selected through BPMN-02/09 and applicable BPMN-06 rules. BPMN-03 uses current offering for new selections; BPMN-04/confirmed records retain agreed schedule. Refresh does not create allocations or alter past paid transactions.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_38_20</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_38_21</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_38" name="Future rules configured; existing commitments preserved">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_38_21</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:userTask id="ReviewError_38" name="Review error/current values; correct, safely retry, or stop">
      <bpmn:documentation>Proposed recovery behavior: retain draft separately. Permission loss requires allowed session; stale version requires reload and explicit review. Invalid fields/rules must be corrected. Retry revalidates the request and never applies a stale overwrite. No fixed retry interval or extra business approval is introduced.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_38_23</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_38_22</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_38_24</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:userTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Recovery_38" name="Owner recovery choice?">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_38_24</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_38_25</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_38_26</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_38_27</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="Stop_38" name="Stopped for now; saved settings/work retained">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_38_26</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_38_17</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Reload_38" name="Reload latest rules/commitments; keep draft separate for review">
      <bpmn:documentation>Refresh after a stale/conflicting save and before retry; preserve unsaved draft separately without silently merging. Current permissions and configuration validity are checked at Load; owner reviews current values in Edit. Reuse any known successful request result where applicable rather than duplicate changes.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_38_27</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_38_28</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
