    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="PoolRules_38">
      <bpmn:text>Separate pool / mandatory rules
Standard: daily varieties and units/variety; default 4 × 10.
Subscription: weekly per product; default 10.
Cake: default 2/week, distinct fulfillment dates.
Positive whole capacity counts.
Standard cutoff: noon at least 1 day before fulfillment, or earlier preparation deadline.
Subscription: noon at least 1 day before first preparation, per lead time.
Cake submission: at least 7 calendar days; timely review is not a new submission.</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:association id="Assoc_PoolRules_38" sourceRef="Validate_38" targetRef="PoolRules_38" associationDirection="None" />
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="Commitments_38">
      <bpmn:text>Preserve committed work
Lower limits may leave existing allocations above the new limit; do not cancel or erase them.
New block prevents NEW bookings, not existing preparation/fulfillment.
Preserve confirmed subscription preparation and fulfillment dates before configuration/schedule edits.
Deactivating an offering stops new enrollments, not prepaid deliveries.
No automatic deferment, hold release, cancellation or refund.</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:association id="Assoc_Commitments_38" sourceRef="Impact_38" targetRef="Commitments_38" associationDirection="None" />
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="Reuse_38">
      <bpmn:text>Rule consumers (separate processes)
BPMN-09: new purchase/resource validation.
BPMN-06: permitted deferment-date capacity check.
BPMN-03: new offering/schedule selection.
BPMN-04: preserved confirmed fulfillment records.
BPMN-30: authentication precondition.
Configuration does not execute any of these workflows.</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:association id="Assoc_Reuse_38" sourceRef="Refresh_38" targetRef="Reuse_38" associationDirection="None" />
